							},
							"paragraphStyle" : {
								"__type" : "textStyle"
							},
							"string" : "- An offset is the running total of the sizes of the live objects, not a memory address. Free chunks are not counted.\n- Indexes and offsets change after every garbage collection, so a window is a picture of one moment.\n- The scans only read the class and the size of each object.\n- The diff follows the first object of each baseline page. A page whose first object has been collected is merged into the page before it.\n\nThe class comments of `ImageMapOverview` and `ImageMapDiff` have the details."
						}
					]
